course: dictionary
lesson: 6050
title: Mental: mind, sums and slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mental is a word with more than one meaning, so the clues around it matter. Its main meaning is to do with the mind: thinking, remembering and feelings. «Try your mental maths: what is 12 groups of 4?» Here you work the sum out in your head, without writing it down.
explain: Read the words around it. «Howay man, divvent be daft, that gadgie was mental» is Geordie for «come on, don't be silly, that bloke was mad». The clues are «divvent be daft», so mental means crazy here. Always ask: what meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Some phrases have a fixed meaning. Mental health is how well your mind and feelings are doing, and a mental picture is a picture you make in your head. Slang like «that ride was mental» is informal, so use it only in friendly talk, and never as an unkind word about someone who is unwell.
fact: Mental means to do with the mind, like thinking, remembering and feelings.
fact: «Mental maths» means working out sums in your head, without writing them down.
fact: «Mental health» means how well your mind and feelings are doing.
fact: In slang, «mental» can mean crazy, wild or amazing, as in «that ride was mental!»
fact: «Mental» was once used as an unkind word for someone who is unwell, so do not use it that way; say «unwell» or «upset» instead.
exercise: Your teacher says, «Today we do mental maths.» What does it mean? | Maths that is crazy and wild | *Working out sums in your head, without writing | Maths done with a ruler and pencil | Maths only done at home
exercise: «That gadgie was mental» means the man was mad. In this slang, what does mental mean? | Sleepy and tired | Clever at sums | Kind and gentle | *Crazy or wild
exercise: «Ella's mental health is good: she sleeps well and laughs with friends.» What does mental health mean? | *How well your mind and feelings are doing | How many books you have read | How fast you can run | How often you visit the dentist
test: Mum says, «Make a mental picture of the castle as I read.» What is a mental picture? | A photo on your phone | A painting hung on a wall | A drawing you colour in | *A picture you make in your head
test: «I'll make a mental note to bring my kit tomorrow.» What does a mental note mean? | A note from the head teacher | A note written in ink | A note you throw away | *Something you remember in your head
exam: Zara says, «That roller coaster was mental!» What does she mean? | Boring and slow | Sad and quiet | Scary because the ride was broken | *Wild and exciting
